yaml/stream
description: A sequence of YAML documents in one file, separated by --- markers
- >
  A **stream** is what a `.yaml` file holds: zero or more documents. `---` starts a document,
  an optional `...` ends one, and a `%YAML` directive may precede a start. Most files hold
  exactly one document and skip the markers altogether:
- !!<format: text/x-yaml> |
  %YAML 1.2
  ---
  first: document
  ...
  ---
  second: document
- >
  Each document's content is a yaml/code - see its chapter:
- *..:01-yaml_code
